# Mock RDI API Conformance

The mock at `mock-rdi-api/app.py` exists to let Redis Insight's RDI tab
work against the local demo. It MUST NOT diverge from the real RDI
control-plane API.

## The rule

Every route exposed by this mock must correspond to a real operation in
<https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/reference/api-reference/>.

If you cannot find a documented operation for a route, **do not add
it** — Insight will not call it in production anyway, and shipping
mock-only endpoints creates false expectations.

## Allowed surface (already implemented)

| Method | Path | Operation in docs |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/v1/login` | `secure_login_api_v1_login_post` |
| GET | `/api/v1/status` | `get_pipeline_status_api_v1_status_get` |
| GET | `/api/v1/pipelines` | `get_pipeline_api_v1_pipelines_get` |
| POST | `/api/v1/pipelines` | `deploy_pipeline_api_v1_pipelines_post` |
| POST | `/api/v1/pipelines/{start,stop,reset}` | lifecycle ops |
| GET | `/api/v1/actions/<id>` | `get_action_api_v1_actions_action_id_get` |
| POST | `/api/v1/pipelines/jobs/dry-run` | `job_dry_run_api_v1_pipelines_jobs_dry_run_post` |
| POST | `/api/v1/pipelines/{targets,sources}/dry-run` | connection test |
| GET | `/api/v1/monitoring/statistics` | analytics |
| GET | `/api/v1/pipelines/{config,jobs}/schemas` | schema for editor |
| GET | `/api/v1/pipelines/strategies` | deployment strategies |
| GET | `/api/v1/pipelines/{config,jobs}/templates/<...>` | starter templates |
| GET | `/api/v1/pipelines/jobs/functions` | JMESPath/SQL function catalog |

## Auth + response contract

- All non-login endpoints must require `Authorization: Bearer <JWT>` (matches the real API's `secure` tag).
- Async lifecycle operations (`/start`, `/stop`, `/reset`, `/pipelines` POST) must return `{ "action_id": "<uuid>" }` immediately, with status polled via `/api/v1/actions/<id>`.
- Schema endpoints must return valid JSON Schema documents that match the YAML keys actually used by `rdi/config.yaml` and `rdi/jobs/*.yaml`.

## After editing

1. Run the endpoint smoke test from `docs/05-rdi-spec-conformance.md`
   §4 — every route should return 200 with a valid JWT.
2. Update `docs/05-rdi-spec-conformance.md` if the route table changed.
3. Re-run `./scripts/verify-redis-enterprise.sh` and confirm
   §8 (RDI control-plane API) still passes.
